WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.300
Modern research operates as a vast
interconnected network involving hundreds

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:10.400
of disciplines, billions in funding, and a
multitude of competing actors.

3
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.500
Within this network, structural tensions
emerge, where an entity's secondary

4
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.680
interests threaten their primary
professional duties.

5
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.480
To navigate these pressures, the BRIGRET
project, co-funded by the European

6
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.800
Union, developed this specific training
module on conflicts of interest.

7
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.020
Managing these complexities requires
moving past static checkbox compliance

8
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:37.960
models. Shifting to a continuous process
of ethical discernment is the most

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.200
effective way to maintain research
integrity in high-stakes environments.

10
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.120
Fostering this ethical awareness is a dual
responsibility shared between two

11
00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.080
primary groups. On one side are the front-
line researchers, from early career

12
00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.840
scientists to senior leads, who navigate
specialized dilemmas in fields like

13
00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.980
AI, data management, and the life
sciences.

14
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.780
On the other side is the institutional
body charged with oversight,

15
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.340
the Research Ethics Committee, or REC.

16
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.900
REC members evaluate specialized protocols
to ensure ethical standards are met

17
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.840
before and during the study. The
interaction between these groups must

18
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.460
function proactively to identify and
anticipate risks.

19
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.420
This ecosystem is designed to bridge the
gap between institutional committee

20
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.380
oversight and the real-world experiences
of researchers in the field.

21
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.820
Neither group can succeed in isolation.

22
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.560
Managing bias depends on this
interconnected, communicative ecosystem

23
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.560
functioning as a unified defense.
